    "Guest studies | Uni Jena\nGuest studies\nErasmus+ and bilateral exchange in Jena\nCampus of the University of Jena\nImage: Christoph Worsch (University of Jena)\nApplication\nShort-term study and research visits for international students\nImage: Christoph Worsch (University of Jena)\nStudy programmes\nfor guest students: courses offered, Learning Agreement, organisation of studies, exams and Transcript of Records\nImage: Christoph Worsch (University of Jena)\nResearch Traineeship\nas an international guest student in Jena\nImage: Christoph Worsch (University of Jena)\nScholarship programmes\nFinancing your study exchange: Erasmus+ and other funding opportunities\nImage: Britta Salheiser (Universität Jena)\nLiving in Jena\nLiving, working, free time –​ information for international students on life in Jena\nImage: Christoph Worsch (University of Jena)\nFAQ - Guest studies\nAnswers to questions frequently asked by guest students\nImage: Christoph Worsch (University of Jena)\nInformation materials\nFlyer Guest Studies\npdf, 1 mb\n· de\nFact Sheet Student Exchange\npdf, 158 kb\n· de\nExperience Reports\nInternational guest students report about their lifes and studies in Jena\nImage: Christoph Worsch (University of Jena)\nShow YouTube video\nplaceholder image — Discover Jena Video Thumbnail\nGraphic: Thomas Franke-Opitz\nHello Jena: The Beginning of Guest Studies\nIn this episode an exchange student talks about her experiences at the beginning of her stay in Jena and the start of the semester.\nHow to prepare? What was a suprise? How is studying in Germany different?\nGraphic: Sabine Müller\n·\nAudio: University of Jena\nYour browser cannot play this file.\nDownload file\nGet to know international students and important information in our podcast \"\nUni Jena international\n\".\n306° Tour of Jena\nExternal link\nClick your way across Jena and discover its beautiful spots virtually!\nScreenshot: Friedrich-Schiller-Universität Jena\nMany Good Reasons to Study in Jena\nNo tuition fees, an international campus with tradition and excellent carrer opportunities - Learn more about the reasons for why Jena is the perfect choice for your studies.\nImage: Nadine Mrosewski\nUniStartJena App\nWith the app \"UniStartJena\" you have all the information you need about the university and the city, Friedolin, the canteen menu, the bus timetable and the events calendar in one app. In German and English. Free of charge.\nImage: Christoph Worsch (University of Jena)\nContact\nInternational Office: International Students\nUniversity Main Building, Room 0.17\nFürstengraben 1\n07743 Jena\nGoogle Maps site plan\nExternal link\nEmail\nincoming@uni-jena.de\nLink to download vCard\nvCard\nFurther link\nMore information\nOffice hours:\nPlease see the telephone office hours of our team members by clicking on \"more information\" on the left.\nShare this page\nShare this page via email\nShare this page via WhatsApp\nShare this page on Facebook\nShare this page on LinkedIn\nShare this page\nTop of the page"
